WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:07.000
You think you've explored medicine. In reality, you're standing in the parking lot of Disney World bragging about how fun

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.540
the pavement is. You've taken pictures of the asphalt. You've written dissertations about the parking stripes.

3
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:21.750
You've never gone inside. After a century of pharmacology, most beneficial effects of molecules on diseases remain unexplored.

4
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:30.600
Not because biology is constrained. Because clinical trials are slow, expensive, and run by people who think "urgency" is

5
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:36.900
a type of perfume. Here's the math. It's painful but brief, like a flu shot administered by someone who hates you.

6
00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:46.880
Your Tiny Sandbox. Here is everything humanity considers "medicine" after five thousand years of civilization: There are

7
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:53.820
twenty thousand products approved in the U.S., which sounds impressive until you realize most are just "Tylenol, but blue."

8
00:00:54.920 --> 00:01:02.220
These products contain only one thousand six hundred and fifty unique compounds, which is fewer ingredients than a decent

9
00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:09.240
French bakery uses. Seven thousand five hundred investigational compounds have passed Phase One globally.

10
00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:18.920
The F.D.A. Generally Recognized As Safe, or G.R.A.S., list contains six hundred and thirty-five substances you could eat

11
00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:26.900
right now without dying. Total unique compounds humanity knows are safe-ish: nine thousand five hundred compounds.

12
00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:32.260
That's it. That's your entire medicine cabinet after five millennia.

13
00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:40.360
The Target List (Ways Your Body Breaks). The International Classification of Diseases, or I.C.D.

14
00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:46.480
ten, lists fourteen thousand ways your meat can malfunction, and you're ignoring it.

15
00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:54.240
After consolidation, there are only one thousand trial-relevant diseases worth actually fixing.

16
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.900
The Math You're Ignoring. Take your nine thousand five hundred safe compounds.

17
00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:06.520
Multiply by one thousand diseases. This gives you the "Combinatorial Space," which is fancy talk for "stuff you could test

18
00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:12.360
tomorrow if you weren't busy filling out forms." (requires many papers) Nine thousand five hundred compounds multiplied

19
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:19.960
by one thousand diseases equals nine million five hundred thousand plausible drug-condition combinations.

20
00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:28.300
What You've Actually Tested. There are one thousand seven hundred and fifty unique approved drug-disease pairings, which

21
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:36.580
make up your entire medical canon. Thirty percent of drugs gain at least one new indication after initial approval, while

22
00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:44.200
the rest never get a second date. Let's be generous and say you tested ten times as many things that failed (You did.

23
00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:50.140
You learned nothing from them.). Total tested: thirty-two thousand five hundred relationships.

24
00:02:51.340 --> 00:03:00.100
The Scorecard. Thirty-two thousand five hundred relationships tested divided by nine million five hundred thousand possibilities

25
00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:10.120
equals zero point three four two percent. where: Humanity has explored less than one percent of the theoretically testable

26
00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:15.600
drug-disease space. You are the detective who searched one drawer and declared the case cold.

27
00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:21.520
It's like reading the first page of *War and Peace* and writing a book report called "It's About a Party."

28
00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:27.760
Technically accurate. Cosmically insufficient. Is The Untested Stuff Useful?

29
00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:31.660
You might argue, "Maybe the other ninety-nine percent is useless!".

30
00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:40.240
Biology would like a word. Mapping three hundred and fifty thousand plus clinical trials showed that only twelve percent

31
00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:47.640
of the human interactome has ever been targeted by drugs. You're ignoring eighty-eight percent of your own biology.

32
00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.900
It's like having a one hundred-room mansion and living exclusively in the bathroom.

33
00:03:54.240 --> 00:04:00.860
Drugs are messy. They hit multiple targets. F.D.A.-approved drugs often bind to things you didn't intend.

34
00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:07.060
This means "side effects" are frequently "cures for something else" that nobody bothered to notice.

35
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:16.860
Sildenafil was developed for chest pain. It failed. Its "side effect" became Viagra, then got repurposed *again* for pulmonary

36
00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:25.480
hypertension. Thalidomide was pulled for causing birth defects; its immunomodulatory "side effects" turned out to treat

37
00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:32.120
multiple myeloma. Two drugs. Three accidental cures. Zero systematic searches.

38
00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:39.080
You keep finding cures by tripping over them in hallways. Imagine if you opened a door on purpose.

39
00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:47.400
Diseases cluster on shared biological networks. Arthritis and Alzheimer's share biological pathways.

40
00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:54.320
Lithium was prescribed for gout in the eighteen hundreds; decades later, it turned out to be the gold standard treatment

41
00:04:54.320 --> 00:05:00.240
for bipolar disorder. Nobody connected the dots because nobody was drawing lines between diseases.

42
00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:06.540
The drug that treats your grandfather's inflammation might fix your grandmother's neurodegeneration.

43
00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:13.240
You won't find out, because testing it would require paperwork that takes longer than Grandma has left.

44
00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:21.600
The Universe is Big. You Are Small. So far we only counted molecules humanity *already has*.

45
00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:26.590
The stuff in your cupboards. If you look at what's chemically possible, it gets embarrassing.

46
00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:34.170
Estimated ten to the power of twenty-three to ten to the power of sixty drug-like molecules.

47
00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:39.330
That's more candidates than there are atoms in your body. Or stars in the galaxy.

48
00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:48.460
Or excuses from your regulatory agencies. Z.I.N.C. twenty-two contains tens of billions of purchasable virtual molecules.

49
00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:57.060
You could order them online. You haven't. You have made less than ten to the power of negative forty of possible molecules.

50
00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:05.780
Tested divided by possible is approximately ten to the power of negative twenty to ten to the power of negative fifty.

51
00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:15.260
Effectively zero. You haven't even started. This is like exploring Earth by looking at one grain of sand on one beach in

52
00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:19.460
New Jersey, then declaring you've "seen the world." You haven't.

53
00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:25.000
You've seen a grain of sand. In New Jersey. Why You Are Still Sick.

54
00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:30.980
It's not because science is hard. It's because you've built a system that is allergic to answers.

55
00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:41.500
One. Trials Cost Too Much: A typical Phase Two to Three randomized controlled trials, or R.C.T.s, costs thirty to one hundred

56
00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:45.820
million dollars (Median cost per patient forty-one thousand dollars).

57
00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:51.920
At that price, you only test "sure things." Safe bets. Boring bets.

58
00:06:52.980 --> 00:07:00.740
Bets that don't cure cancer. Clinical trials are a velvet-rope nightclub where the bouncer is a regulatory agency and the

59
00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:09.320
cover charge is a hundred million dollars. Herd Mentality: Trials overwhelmingly test the same few biological targets due

60
00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:15.820
to preferential attachment dynamics. Everyone studies what everyone else studies because that's how you get grants.

61
00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:22.240
It's like if every explorer only went to France because France already had good reviews on TripAdvisor.

62
00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:28.060
Meanwhile, undiscovered continents full of cures sit there, undiscovered.

63
00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:38.450
No Profit: Most molecules have no patent. No patent equals no one hundred million dollar trial equals no approval.

64
00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:46.100
Metformin, a diabetes drug from the nineteen fifties, shows persistent signals for reducing cancer risk and extending lifespan.

65
00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:56.000
It costs pennies. It's off-patent. The trial to prove it works for aging (Targeting Aging with Metformin, or T.A.M.E.) spent

66
00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:01.800
years begging for funding because no pharmaceutical company will bankroll a drug they can't monopolize.

67
00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:07.840
The molecule that saves your life has to make money first. If it can't, it won't.

68
00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:16.400
You die. Quarterly earnings go up. Neglect: If you have a rare disease with no market, you don't get a drug.

69
00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:24.680
Your cells malfunction in an unprofitable way. The invisible hand of the market has weighed your life against quarterly

70
00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:30.350
earnings and found you wanting. Sorry about your death. It was a business decision.

71
00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:39.039
How Long to Explore Everything? At the current pace of three thousand three hundred trials per year, how long would it take

72
00:08:39.039 --> 00:08:45.600
to systematically test therapeutic possibilities? Tier 1: Single Compounds (Most Conservative).

73
00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:55.080
Testing every known safe compound against every major disease: Nine point five million combinations divided by three thousand

74
00:08:55.080 --> 00:09:00.220
three hundred trials per year equals two thousand eight hundred and eighty years.

75
00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:06.880
That's almost three thousand years to explore compounds we *already know are safe*.

76
00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:10.510
By that math, we won't finish until the year five thousand.

77
00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:19.320
Tier 2: Combination Therapies (Still Defensible). Modern medicine increasingly relies on multi-drug cocktails.

78
00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:25.840
Oncology, H.I.V., cardiology, psychiatry: all routinely use drug combinations.

79
00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:32.260
So the real question isn't "does this one drug work?" It's "which combinations work?"

80
00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:41.840
Testing pairwise combinations of safe compounds: Forty-five point one billion combinations divided by three thousand three

81
00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:46.860
hundred trials per year equals thirteen point seven million years.

82
00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:51.290
That's longer than *Homo sapiens* has existed as a species.

83
00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:57.680
And that's using only compounds with established safety data, testing only pairs.

84
00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:05.040
Not triplets. God help you if you want to try triplets. Tier 3: The Full Chemical Universe (Illustrative).

85
00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:14.360
Beyond known compounds lies the chemical space of ten to the twenty-third power to ten to the sixtieth power drug-like molecules.

86
00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:22.040
At current trial capacity, exploring even the *synthesizable* fraction would take longer than the universe has existed.

87
00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:28.060
The universe is thirteen point eight billion years old. You need more time than that.

88
00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:35.180
To test pills. Pills that already exist. We haven't even started.

89
00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:43.860
"But Won't We Run Out of Easy Discoveries?". Some will argue "diminishing returns": the more we search, the harder each

90
00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:48.580
new discovery becomes. This assumes we've already picked the low-hanging fruit.

91
00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:54.210
We haven't picked *any* fruit. We're still in the parking lot arguing about whether fruit exists.

92
00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.360
Diminishing returns only kicks in after you've explored a significant fraction of the space.

93
00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:06.700
At less than one percent explored, every trial teaches you something new about human biology, improving your ability to

94
00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:11.820
predict what works next. Learning compounds. Depletion is negligible.

95
00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:17.040
You are nowhere near the bottom of the barrel because you have not yet located the barrel.

96
00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:25.220
The math: even with weak learning, diminishing returns only matters after exploring roughly thirty-seven percent of therapeutic

97
00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:31.860
space. For combination therapies, that crossover is roughly seven million years away at current pace.

98
00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:36.080
You cannot have diminishing returns when you've barely started looking.

99
00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:46.120
See the formal analysis for the equations. The Fix. The Oxford RECOVERY Trial (COVID nineteen) proved that large-scale pragmatic

100
00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:51.800
trials can run for roughly five hundred dollars and deliver results in less than one hundred days.

101
00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:57.100
Five hundred dollars versus forty-one thousand dollars. Read those numbers again.

102
00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:05.980
One of them is the reason people are dying. With a decentralized D.F.D.A., trial capacity increases by twelve point three

103
00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:13.700
times: Nine point five million combinations divided by forty thousand seven hundred trials per year equals two hundred and

104
00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:19.200
thirty-four years. Still a long time, but at least it's a number with fewer digits than a phone book.

105
00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:25.880
And the first few decades would capture the highest-value discoveries (the low-hanging fruit that current trial scarcity

106
00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:29.080
forces you to ignore while people die in the waiting room).

107
00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:37.340
More importantly, your decentralized D.F.D.A. builds permanent infrastructure for systematic therapeutic exploration.

108
00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:45.120
The goal isn't to "finish." It's to stop leaving cures on the table while you form subcommittees to discuss whether to form

109
00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:49.160
committees to review the proposal to consider them. The Bottom Line.

110
00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:57.340
Humanity has empirically tested less than one percent of the drug-disease relationships that can be tested using existing

111
00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:06.300
safe compounds. If you include the larger chemical universe, humanity has explored roughly one-quadrillionth to one-quintillionth

112
00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:10.700
of what is possible (ten to the negative twelfth to ten to the negative fiftieth).

113
00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:15.640
There are numbers so small that mathematicians get depressed looking at them.

114
00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:21.650
These are those numbers. The overwhelming majority of therapeutic potential remains untouched.

115
00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:26.680
Not because cures are impossible. Because trials are too expensive and too slow.

116
00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:35.180
A decentralized, automated pragmatic trial system is the only route to systematically explore the remaining ninety-nine

117
00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:42.880
point nine nine nine percent of medical space. You're not in the parking lot because there's nothing inside Disney World.

118
00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:49.500
You're in the parking lot because the entrance fee is one hundred million dollars and requires seventeen years of paperwork.

119
00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:53.370
People are dying in the parking lot. The rides are right there.

120
00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:57.160
You can hear the screaming. (Fun screaming. Cure screaming.).

121
00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.600
The cures are inside. Open the gate.
